cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite it and the accompanying paper."
title: "What Formalization and Internal Review Changed: A Case Study in Subsistence-Risk Adoption"
url: "https://github.com/AgrEconLab/AIClimateFoodSecurity"
authors:
  - name: "EconLean contributors"
date-released: "2026-10-25"
version: "0.7.0"
abstract: >-
  A methodology case study of a Lean 4 formalization of a subsistence-risk
  technology-adoption model. The paper documents what machine-checking changed
  in the claim set (characterizations, identities, argmax accounting, and
  examples), maps prose assumptions to their Lean encodings, and proposes a
  formalization-delta protocol. The artifact contains the Lean 4 formalization,
  the farmer and benchmark problems, two two-state examples, a
  binding-liquidity variant, and a numerical illustration.
keywords:
  - AI adoption
  - climate risk
  - food security
  - subsistence income risk
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - benchmark
  - QuantEcon
  - policy simulation
license: "Apache-2.0"
